%description:

The sectors of a site differ by their antenna patterns, and by nothing else.

TR 38.901 7.5 Step 4: "the LSPs for links from co-sited sectors to a UT are
the same"; shadow fading is one of them, and the LOS state of Step 2 is the
site's too. So the ratio of the powers a UE receives from two sectors of one
site is the ratio of the two antenna patterns towards it. A model that draws
the shadowing per cell adds the difference of two draws to that ratio: a
standard deviation of 8.5 dB in an urban macrocell.

The scenario is the three-sector site of simulations/nr/three_sector: three
gNBs at one position with one site name, their sectors 120 degrees apart. The
victim UE stands on the boundary of two sectors, 60 degrees off both
boresights, and is served by one of them; a UE in each of the other two
sectors keeps its sector busy. Shadowing and the per-link LOS draw are on,
the fast fading is off, and the thermal noise is set far below everything
(-300 dBm), so the SINR the victim measures is a ratio of received powers:

    SINR = S1 / (S2 + S3)

with all three over the same path loss, LOS state and shadowing. With both
other sectors on the band, the lowest SINR measured is therefore

    -A(60 deg) - 10 log10( 10^(-A(60 deg)/10) + 10^(-A(180 deg)/10) )

where A is the antenna pattern of TR 36.873 Table 7.1-1 towards the victim:
about 0 dB, whatever the seed. The run is repeated with four seeds, and a
tripwire checks that the seeds are different realizations (the quiet SINR,
over the noise alone, differs between them).

Characterisation on one point: the model takes the pattern of TR 36.873 for
a TR 38.901 cell, which the grader reproduces.

%extraargs: -c ThreeSectorSite

%file: demo.xml
<config>
    <interface among='eNB* eNodeB* enb* *Enb* gNB* gNodeB* gnb* *Gnb* upf* *Upf* mecHost* pgw*' address='10.x.x.x' netmask='255.255.255.0'/>
    <interface hosts='*' address='192.168.x.x' netmask='255.255.255.0'/>
</config>

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[Config ThreeSectorSite]
network = simu5g.simulations.nr.networks.ThreeSectorSite_Standalone
# the positions this test gives the nodes are their antennas': no height offset
**.antenna.mobility.offsetZ = 0m
sim-time-limit = 3s
**.routingRecorder.enabled = false
cmdenv-express-mode = true
cmdenv-status-frequency = 10000000s
**.sctp.**.scalar-recording = false
**.sctp.nagleEnabled = false
**.sctp.enableHeartbeats = false

output-scalar-file = results/${iterationvarsf}${repetition}.sca
output-vector-file = results/${iterationvarsf}${repetition}.vec
**.vector-recording = false
**.measuredSinrDl.result-recording-modes = mean,count,min,max

############### The sweep: four realizations ##############
seed-set = ${seed = 0, 1, 2, 3}

############### The site: three sectors at one position ##############
*.gnb1.mobility.initialX = 1000m
*.gnb1.mobility.initialY = 1000m
*.gnb1.mobility.initialZ = 25m
*.gnb2.mobility.initialX = 1000m
*.gnb2.mobility.initialY = 1000m
*.gnb2.mobility.initialZ = 25m
*.gnb3.mobility.initialX = 1000m
*.gnb3.mobility.initialY = 1000m
*.gnb3.mobility.initialZ = 25m
*.gnb*.site = "site1"
*.gnb*.cellularNic.antenna.txDirection = "ANISOTROPIC"
*.gnb1.cellularNic.antenna.txAngle = 120deg
*.gnb2.cellularNic.antenna.txAngle = 240deg
*.gnb3.cellularNic.antenna.txAngle = 0deg

############### The UEs ##############
# The victim is due west of the mast, 60 degrees off the boresights of gnb1
# and gnb2 and behind gnb3; the other two UEs are on the boresights of gnb2
# and gnb3. The associations are fixed.
*.numUe = 3
*.ue[*].servingNodeId = 0
*.ue[0].nrServingNodeId = 1
*.ue[1].nrServingNodeId = 2
*.ue[2].nrServingNodeId = 3
**.dynamicCellAssociation = false
**.enableHandover = false
*.ue[0].mobility.initialX = 800m
*.ue[0].mobility.initialY = 1000m
*.ue[0].mobility.initialZ = 1.5m
*.ue[1].mobility.initialX = 900m
*.ue[1].mobility.initialY = 826.8m
*.ue[2].mobility.initialX = 1200m
*.ue[2].mobility.initialY = 1000m
*.ue[1..2].mobility.initialZ = 1.5m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinX = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinY = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinZ = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxX = 2000m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxY = 2000m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxZ = 50m
**.mobility.initFromDisplayString = false

############### The channel: the site's large-scale state, and no noise to speak of ##############
*.gnb*.scenario = "URBAN_MACROCELL"
**.dynamicLos = true
**.shadowing = true
**.fading = false
**.downlinkInterference = true
**.uplinkInterference = false
**.bgCellInterference = false
**.extCellInterference = false
**.thermalNoise = -300dBm

*.carrierAggregation.numComponentCarriers = 1
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].carrierFrequency = 2GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].numResourceBlocks = 6
**.numResourceBlocks = 6
**.eNodeBTxPower = 40dBm
*.gnb*.cellularNic.antenna.gain = 18dBi
*.ue[*].cellularNic.antenna.gain = 0dBi
**.cableLoss = 2dB

############### X2: the mesh of the three sectors ##############
*.gnb*.numX2Apps = 2
*.gnb*.x2App[*].server.localPort = 5000 + ancestorIndex(1)
*.gnb1.x2App[0].client.connectAddress = "gnb2%x2ppp0"
*.gnb1.x2App[1].client.connectAddress = "gnb3%x2ppp0"
*.gnb2.x2App[0].client.connectAddress = "gnb1%x2ppp0"
*.gnb2.x2App[1].client.connectAddress = "gnb3%x2ppp1"
*.gnb3.x2App[0].client.connectAddress = "gnb1%x2ppp1"
*.gnb3.x2App[1].client.connectAddress = "gnb2%x2ppp1"

############### Traffic: a trickle to the victim, a flood to the other two sectors ##############
*.ue[*].numApps = 1
*.server.numApps = 3
*.ue[*].app[0].typename = "CbrReceiver"
*.ue[*].app[0].localPort = 3000
*.server.app[*].typename = "CbrSender"
*.server.app[*].destPort = 3000
*.server.app[*].localPort = 3088 + ancestorIndex(0)
*.server.app[0].destAddress = "ue[0]"
*.server.app[0].packetSize = 40B
*.server.app[0].samplingTime = 0.02s
*.server.app[0].startTime = 0.1s
# The floods start late, so that the victim also measures a quiet channel
*.server.app[1..2].destAddress = "ue[" + string(ancestorIndex(0)) + "]"
*.server.app[1..2].packetSize = 1000B
*.server.app[1..2].samplingTime = 0.0002s
*.server.app[1..2].startTime = 1s

*.configurator.config = xmldoc("./demo.xml")

%postrun-command: ../../physics_reference.py --grade results >verdict.txt

%contains: verdict.txt
graded=8 failures=0

%not-contains: verdict.txt
FAILED
